  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_fbc1b27efb2048edb4821931a4a607a1",
      "statement": "The pre-push hook is the only place the site linter and the knowledge-bundle checker become enforcement rather than scripts, running both against the repository root and aborting the push when either exits non-zero.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.githooks/pre-push#L32-L66",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e6511d9f6925e77c20986bf4021b15c5b1b6b3de9c9b7291f6241b4afa080a16:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_859176c723bc4df084c92bf76660bff9",
      "statement": "The hook fails open in two cases, exiting 0 when _tools/site_lint.py is absent and when no python3 interpreter can be located, so a missing prerequisite silently disables the gate instead of blocking the push.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.githooks/pre-push#L35-L46",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:729c284494065062a8cbf7f607ed08a8330686b4eeb928718895d725cc6882a1:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_eb4c7c7342164f7ba470b4c67ac74e44",
      "statement": "The hook file is tracked by git but the core.hooksPath setting that activates it is not, so every fresh clone pushes unguarded until the setting is applied by hand.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.githooks/pre-push#L24-L30",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:78f33249c3e22249c538bfb5bc6b38e30e874a4eaa51f225ba20c6b1a15065f7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_47f614507cb540dc9f87aef4b7aaf892",
      "statement": "The knowledge-bundle check is bound to the push gate rather than the site publish workflow because knowledge/ is never published, and coupling a broken concept card to a site deployment would be the wrong dependency.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.githooks/pre-push#L8-L11",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:86ea714967d0fdf82333796435a6f9a12a9bb276887de1096da38a75a152c4be:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/adr/0002-knowledge-bundle-scope-and-gate.md#L24-L34",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:aedb310f0a5af2d10e5464916f8638121a51d181deee136e7d9e6786af3733c6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8a1039a5f5ed445298d60f982a160bc2",
      "statement": "The gate blocks errors and deliberately passes warnings, because a style quota that could block a push would contradict the repository's own editorial rule that a third-tier fix must be abandoned when it makes the sentence worse.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.githooks/pre-push#L12-L19",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f7bb5fa2d7d06370dde0292f567f238ce4ddc3b3a343a9e15b71d60c0b39fc48:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_19d6c8081b464f659a5353ccfe44ab8b",
      "statement": "The bundle check is wrapped in an existence test, so a missing checker file is skipped silently and is a third fail-open branch distinct from the two that print a message before exiting.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.githooks/pre-push#L56-L66",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f4bf848627f3e2b476298a74391e93bea9ecb4facf2b1362955a6b08293b02e8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_cb6ef9be1cc44919b176a233dae2fa4c",
      "statement": "Nothing in the repository invokes the bundle checker's selftest automatically; the hook deliberately omits it because a push carries content rather than the checker's own correctness, and wiring it to CI is recorded as a future condition rather than current behavior.",
      "evidence": [
